    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (81.41) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03), both of whom benefit immensely from high-leverage spots in their respective orders and favorable matchups against back-end starters. **Corbin Carroll** remains our elite engine; his speed-first profile combined with a strong xwOBA against Lorenzen makes him a must-start, while **Tyler Soderstrom** offers massive upside hitting into the 5-hole against Giolito. **Brice Turang** (72.43) also earns a premium spot today; despite the challenging prospect of facing Sasaki, the combination of his likely #2 order placement and an elevated SP_xERA for the opponent boosts his efficiency score well into the \"Strong\" territory. **James Wood** (70.10) rounds out the top tier, as his #1 spot in the order provides a volume floor that makes him virtually untouchable in our lineup configurations.\n\nThe bench decision process was tightest around **Kyle Karros** (51.91), who hovered right near the marginal threshold but ultimately failed to crack the starting nine. The optimizer favored the higher ceiling of **Henry Bolte** (53.60) in the outfield rotation, despite **Henry Bolte** facing the same difficult Giolito matchup as **Tyler Soderstrom**. Conversely, **Travis Bazzana** (39.66) was excluded entirely as he fell below our \"Zebras Floor\" of 40.0; his matchup against Wheeler is a brutal assignment that suppresses his value across all five categories. We are also managing health and environmental volatility, with **Mickey Moniak** remaining sidelined on the IL and **Jose Caballero** ruled out due to a rainout.\n\nLooking ahead, we are tracking the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing** closely. **Gabriel Moreno** maintains a respectable 57.97, but any demotion in the batting order below his projected #7 spot could necessitate a pivot to preserve our game caps. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (60.32) is a fascinating play today; while Kirby represents an elite arm, the heavy platoon advantage (+14%) boosts **Vinnie Pasquantino** above the \"Strong\" floor, making him an efficient utilization of our utility slot. We remain vigilant on the weather and official lineups, as even minor adjustments to these projected spots could shift the daily efficiency of **Josh Naylor** and **Austin Riley**, both of whom are currently projected to provide stable, reliable production.",
